;; THE HUMAN GATES OF A STAGE, AS A RECORD - a file, not a status line in prose, so that
;; `bb next` can read where the stage stands the way the loop reads a merge decision. Copy to
;; `stage-N-gates.edn` beside the stage plan when the stage is pulled. Each gate is nil until
;; the person passes it, then a map with the date; nothing but the person writes one, and a
;; gate once passed is not unpassed - a stage that loops back re-runs its exit criteria and
;; closes again with a later date. Three gates for every stage, and a fourth for a pre-release
;; stage.
{:stage/id "<N>"
 ;; the stage plan approved, with its cap (the plan's §11): {:date "YYYY-MM-DD" :cap "<$>" :by "the person"}
 :stage/approved nil
 ;; the blueprint signed off (workflow step 10): {:date "YYYY-MM-DD" :by "the person"}
 :blueprint/signed nil
 ;; A PRE-RELEASE STAGE ONLY: the threat model signed - every line of 02-architecture.md §15
 ;; answered, each with its evidence (the stage plan's §7): {:date "YYYY-MM-DD" :by "the person"}.
 ;; Another kind leaves it nil; `bb next` asks for it of a pre-release stage, before it closes
 :security/signed nil
 ;; the exit criteria met, deployed locally and walked (the plan's §11): {:date "YYYY-MM-DD" :mvp? false}
 :stage/closed nil}
